#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:4
msgid "Landau理論と相転移の次数"
msgstr "Landau Theory and the Order of Phase Transitions"

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:6
msgid ""
"高温相で0、低温相で0でない量を **秩序変数** と呼ぶ。構造相転移では\\ :ref:`ソフトモードの振幅<sm-landau>`\\ が、 "
"強誘電転移では\\ :ref:`自発分極<spontaneous-polarization>`\\ "
"が秩序変数になる。Landau理論では、自由エネルギーを "
"秩序変数の多項式で展開し、2次の係数だけが温度とともに符号を変えると仮定する。本稿では、この展開から、 "
"秩序変数が連続的に育つ2次転移と、転移点で跳ぶ1次転移を導き、1次転移で現れる準安定な状態と、加熱と冷却で "
"転移温度がずれる理由を説明する。最後に、秩序変数に共役な場への応答から、Curie–Weissの法則を導く。"
msgstr ""
"A quantity that is zero in the high-temperature phase and nonzero in the "
"low-temperature phase is called an **order parameter**. In a structural "
"phase transition, the \\ :ref:`soft-mode amplitude <sm-landau>`\\  serves"
" as the order parameter, and in a ferroelectric transition, the \\ "
":ref:`spontaneous polarization <spontaneous-polarization>`\\  plays that "
"role. Landau theory expands the free energy as a polynomial in the order "
"parameter and assumes that only the quadratic coefficient changes sign "
"with temperature. From this expansion we derive second-order transitions,"
" in which the order parameter grows continuously, and first-order "
"transitions, in which it jumps at the transition. We explain the "
"metastable states that arise in a first-order transition and why the "
"transition temperatures on heating and cooling can differ. Finally, we "
"derive the Curie–Weiss law from the response to a field conjugate to the "
"order parameter."

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:12
msgid ""
"**前提知識**: :ref:`ソフトモードと構造相転移<soft-mode>`\\ （とくに\\ :ref:`秩序変数としてのモードの振幅"
"<sm-landau>`\\ と \\ :ref:`+Qと−Qの等価性<sm-inversion-equivalence>`）、 "
"一定温度では自由エネルギーが最小の状態が実現すること。"
msgstr ""
"**Prerequisites**: :ref:`Soft Modes and Structural Phase Transitions "
"<soft-mode>`\\  (especially \\ :ref:`Mode Amplitude as an Order Parameter"
" <sm-landau>`\\  and \\ :ref:`Equivalence of +Q and −Q and Inversion "
"Symmetry <sm-inversion-equivalence>`), and the fact that at a given "
"temperature the state with the lowest free energy is realized."

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:16
msgid "**学習目標**:"
msgstr "**Learning objectives**:"

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:18
msgid "秩序変数で自由エネルギーを展開し、2次転移で秩序変数が転移温度から連続的に育つことを導く。"
msgstr ""
"Expand the free energy in the order parameter and derive how the order "
"parameter grows continuously from the transition temperature in a second-"
"order transition."

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:19
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"4次の係数が負のとき1次転移になることを示し、転移温度 :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` と :math:`T_0` "
"の差、転移点での秩序変数の跳びを導く。"
msgstr ""
"Show that a negative quartic coefficient gives a first-order transition, "
"and derive both the difference between the transition temperature "
":math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` and :math:`T_0` and the jump in the order "
"parameter at the transition."

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:20
msgid "過冷却・過熱が起こりうる温度範囲を求め、加熱と冷却で転移温度がずれる理由を説明する。"
msgstr ""
"Find the temperature ranges in which supercooling and superheating are "
"possible and explain why the transition temperatures on heating and "
"cooling differ."

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:21
msgid "秩序変数に共役な場への応答から、Curie–Weissの法則を導く。"
msgstr ""
"Derive the Curie–Weiss law from the response to a field conjugate to the "
"order parameter."

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:26
msgid "秩序変数による自由エネルギーの展開"
msgstr "Expanding the Free Energy in the Order Parameter"

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:28
msgid "秩序変数を :math:`\\eta` と書く。高温相のまわりで、単位体積あたりの自由エネルギーを :math:`\\eta` で展開して"
msgstr ""
"Write the order parameter as :math:`\\eta`. Expand the free energy per "
"unit volume in powers of :math:`\\eta` about the high-temperature phase:"

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:30
msgid ""
"F(\\eta,T)=F_0(T)+\\frac12a(T-T_0)\\,\\eta^2+\\frac14\\beta\\,\\eta^4+\\frac16\\gamma\\,\\eta^6\\qquad(a>0,\\"
" \\gamma>0)"
msgstr ""
"F(\\eta,T)=F_0(T)+\\frac12a(T-T_0)\\,\\eta^2+\\frac14\\beta\\,\\eta^4+\\frac16\\gamma\\,\\eta^6\\qquad(a>0,\\"
" \\gamma>0)"

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:35
msgid ""
"と置く。奇数次の項がないのは、高温相の対称性で :math:`\\eta` と :math:`-\\eta` が\\ :ref:`等価になる"
"<sm-inversion-equivalence>`\\ からである。 Landau理論の仮定は、2次の係数だけが "
":math:`a(T-T_0)` と温度に比例して符号を変え、:math:`\\beta` と :math:`\\gamma` は "
"転移の近くで温度によらないとすることである。各温度で :math:`F` を最小にする :math:`\\eta=\\eta_0` "
"が、その温度で実現する 状態を表す。"
msgstr ""
"There are no odd-order terms because :math:`\\eta` and :math:`-\\eta` are"
" \\ :ref:`equivalent <sm-inversion-equivalence>`\\  by symmetry of the "
"high-temperature phase. Landau theory assumes that only the quadratic "
"coefficient, :math:`a(T-T_0)`, varies linearly with temperature and "
"changes sign, and that :math:`\\beta` and :math:`\\gamma` are independent"
" of temperature near the transition. At each temperature, the value that "
"minimizes :math:`F`, :math:`\\eta=\\eta_0`, represents the state realized"
" at that temperature."

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:40
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
":math:`\\eta` をソフトモードの振幅 :math:`Q` とすると、0 Kのエネルギーの展開 :eq:`sm-landau` "
"の2次の係数 :math:`\\kappa` は、 調和近似でのモードの振動数の2乗 :math:`\\omega_{\\mathrm s}^2`"
" である。ただし :eq:`sm-landau` は単位胞あたりのエネルギーで、 :math:`Q` "
"も単位胞あたりの質量重み付きの振幅なので、単位体積あたりの :math:`F` と比べるときは単位胞の体積 :math:`\\Omega` "
"を掛ける。 体積を固定すると :math:`\\omega_{\\mathrm "
"s}^2=\\Omega\\,\\partial^2F/\\partial Q^2` である。Landau理論は "
":math:`\\kappa=\\Omega a(T-T_0)` と置き、 "
"有限温度の平均的な復元力が温度とともに変わることを表す。:math:`\\eta` を分極 :math:`P` "
"とすると、Devonshireが強誘電体に 用いた展開になる [Devonshire1949]_。"
msgstr ""
"If :math:`\\eta` is the soft-mode amplitude :math:`Q`, the coefficient of"
" the quadratic term in the 0 K energy expansion (Equation :eq:`sm-"
"landau`), :math:`\\kappa`, is the squared mode frequency "
":math:`\\omega_{\\mathrm s}^2` in the harmonic approximation. However, "
"Equation :eq:`sm-landau` gives the energy per unit cell, and :math:`Q` is"
" also a mass-weighted amplitude per unit cell. When comparing with "
":math:`F` per unit volume, multiply by the unit-cell volume "
":math:`\\Omega`. At fixed volume, :math:`\\omega_{\\mathrm "
"s}^2=\\Omega\\,\\partial^2F/\\partial Q^2`. Landau theory sets "
":math:`\\kappa=\\Omega a(T-T_0)` to express the temperature dependence of"
" the average restoring force at finite temperature. Taking :math:`\\eta` "
"to be the polarization :math:`P` gives the expansion that Devonshire used"
" for ferroelectrics [Devonshire1949]_."

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:50
msgid "2次転移"
msgstr "Second-Order Transition"

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:52
msgid ""
":math:`\\beta>0` の場合を考え、6次の項を省く。:math:`\\partial "
"F/\\partial\\eta=a(T-T_0)\\eta+\\beta\\eta^3=0` から、 :math:`T>T_0` では極小は "
":math:`\\eta_0=0` だけで、高温相が安定である。:math:`T<T_0` では :math:`\\eta=0` が極大になり、"
msgstr ""
"Consider :math:`\\beta>0` and omit the sixth-order term. From "
":math:`\\partial F/\\partial\\eta=a(T-T_0)\\eta+\\beta\\eta^3=0`, for "
":math:`T>T_0` the only minimum is at :math:`\\eta_0=0` and the high-"
"temperature phase is stable. For :math:`T<T_0`, :math:`\\eta=0` becomes a"
" maximum and minima appear at"

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:55
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\eta_0^2=\\frac{a(T_0-T)}{\\beta}"
msgstr "\\eta_0^2=\\frac{a(T_0-T)}{\\beta}"

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:60
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"に極小が現れる。秩序変数は :math:`T_0` から :math:`\\sqrt{T_0-T}` "
"に比例して連続的に育つ。このように秩序変数が連続的に 変わる転移を **2次転移**\\ （連続転移）と呼び、転移温度は "
":math:`T_{\\mathrm C}=T_0` である。"
msgstr ""
"The order parameter grows continuously as the temperature drops below "
":math:`T_0`, in proportion to :math:`\\sqrt{T_0-T}`. A transition in "
"which the order parameter changes continuously is called a **second-order"
" transition**\\  (a continuous transition), with transition temperature "
":math:`T_{\\mathrm C}=T_0`."

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:63
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
":math:`\\eta=Q` のとき、極小のまわりの曲率に単位胞の体積を掛けた "
":math:`\\Omega\\,\\partial^2F/\\partial Q^2` が、ソフトモードの振動数の2乗を与える。 "
":math:`T>T_0` では :math:`\\omega_{\\mathrm s}^2=\\Omega a(T-T_0)` で、\\ "
":ref:`Cochranの法則<sm-definition>`\\ （式 :eq:`sm-cochran`）に従って転移温度に向かって下がる。 "
":math:`T<T_0` では "
":math:`\\partial^2F/\\partial\\eta^2=a(T-T_0)+3\\beta\\eta_0^2=2a(T_0-T)`"
" なので :math:`\\omega_{\\mathrm s}^2=2\\Omega a(T_0-T)` で、振動数の2乗は2倍の傾きで "
"再び増える（:numref:`fig-landau-second-order`）。"
msgstr ""
"When :math:`\\eta=Q`, the curvature around the minimum multiplied by the "
"unit-cell volume, :math:`\\Omega\\,\\partial^2F/\\partial Q^2`, gives the"
" squared soft-mode frequency. For :math:`T>T_0`, the result is "
":math:`\\omega_{\\mathrm s}^2=\\Omega a(T-T_0)`, which decreases toward "
"the transition temperature according to \\ :ref:`Cochran’s law <sm-"
"definition>`\\  (Equation :eq:`sm-cochran`). For :math:`T<T_0`, "
":math:`\\partial^2F/\\partial\\eta^2=a(T-T_0)+3\\beta\\eta_0^2=2a(T_0-T)`"
" gives :math:`\\omega_{\\mathrm s}^2=2\\Omega a(T_0-T)`, so the squared "
"frequency increases again with double the slope magnitude (:numref:`fig-"
"landau-second-order`)."

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:68
msgid "左は秩序変数の温度変化で、T0より上で0、下でT0から平方根の形で増える。右は単位胞の体積を掛けた曲率で、T0の上でΩa(T-T0)、下で2Ωa(T0-T)の直線。"
msgstr ""
"Left: Temperature dependence of the order parameter. It is zero above T0 "
"and grows from T0 with a square-root dependence below it. Right: "
"Curvature multiplied by the unit-cell volume. The straight lines are "
"Ωa(T-T0) above T0 and 2Ωa(T0-T) below it."

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:74
msgid ""
":math:`\\beta>0` の2次転移。左：秩序変数 :math:`\\eta_0`\\ （式 :eq:`landau-second-"
"order`）。右：極小のまわりの曲率に単位胞の体積を掛けた "
":math:`\\Omega\\,\\partial^2F/\\partial\\eta^2`\\ （:math:`\\eta=Q` "
"ならソフトモードの :math:`\\omega^2`）。:math:`T_0` の上（青）は :math:`\\Omega "
"a(T-T_0)`、下（赤）は :math:`2\\Omega a(T_0-T)`。 係数は説明用で、特定の物質の値ではない。"
msgstr ""
"Second-order transition for :math:`\\beta>0`. Left: Order parameter "
":math:`\\eta_0`\\  (Equation :eq:`landau-second-order`). Right: Curvature"
" around a minimum multiplied by the unit-cell volume, "
":math:`\\Omega\\,\\partial^2F/\\partial\\eta^2`\\  (when :math:`\\eta=Q`,"
" this is :math:`\\omega^2` for the soft mode). Above :math:`T_0` the blue"
" line is :math:`\\Omega a(T-T_0)`, and below it the red line is "
":math:`2\\Omega a(T_0-T)`. The coefficients are illustrative and do not "
"represent any particular material."

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:81
msgid "1次転移"
msgstr "First-Order Transition"

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:83
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
":math:`\\beta<0` では、6次の項が大きい :math:`|\\eta|` での壁を作る。:math:`T` が "
":math:`T_0` に下がる前に、:math:`\\eta\\ne0` の極小の 自由エネルギーが :math:`\\eta=0` "
"と等しくなる。その温度が転移温度 :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` で、:math:`F-F_0=0` と "
":math:`\\partial F/\\partial\\eta=0` が同じ :math:`\\eta\\ne0` で成り立つ。それぞれを "
":math:`\\eta^2`、:math:`\\eta` で割ると"
msgstr ""
"For :math:`\\beta<0`, the sixth-order term forms the walls at large "
":math:`|\\eta|`. Before :math:`T` falls to :math:`T_0`, the free energy "
"of the minimum at :math:`\\eta\\ne0` equals that at :math:`\\eta=0`. This"
" occurs at the transition temperature :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}`, where "
":math:`F-F_0=0` and :math:`\\partial F/\\partial\\eta=0` hold for the "
"same nonzero value, :math:`\\eta\\ne0`. Dividing the two equations by "
":math:`\\eta^2` and :math:`\\eta`, respectively, gives"

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:87
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\frac12a(T_{\\mathrm "
"C}-T_0)+\\frac14\\beta\\eta^2+\\frac16\\gamma\\eta^4=0,\\qquad\n"
"a(T_{\\mathrm C}-T_0)+\\beta\\eta^2+\\gamma\\eta^4=0"
msgstr ""
"\\frac12a(T_{\\mathrm "
"C}-T_0)+\\frac14\\beta\\eta^2+\\frac16\\gamma\\eta^4=0,\\qquad\n"
"a(T_{\\mathrm C}-T_0)+\\beta\\eta^2+\\gamma\\eta^4=0"

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:92
msgid ""
"となる。第1式の2倍から第2式を引くと "
":math:`-\\frac12\\beta\\eta^2-\\frac23\\gamma\\eta^4=0`、すなわち "
":math:`\\eta^2=-3\\beta/(4\\gamma)` で、 これを第2式に戻すと"
msgstr ""
"Subtracting the second equation from twice the first gives "
":math:`-\\frac12\\beta\\eta^2-\\frac23\\gamma\\eta^4=0`, or "
":math:`\\eta^2=-3\\beta/(4\\gamma)`. Substituting this into the second "
"equation gives"

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:95
msgid ""
"T_{\\mathrm C}-T_0=\\frac{3\\beta^2}{16a\\gamma}>0,\\qquad\n"
"\\eta_0(T_{\\mathrm C})=\\sqrt{-\\frac{3\\beta}{4\\gamma}}"
msgstr ""
"T_{\\mathrm C}-T_0=\\frac{3\\beta^2}{16a\\gamma}>0,\\qquad\n"
"\\eta_0(T_{\\mathrm C})=\\sqrt{-\\frac{3\\beta}{4\\gamma}}"

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:101
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"を得る。秩序変数は :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` で0から有限の値へ跳ぶ。このように秩序変数が不連続に変わる転移を "
"**1次転移** と呼ぶ。 :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` での :math:`\\eta=0` の曲率 "
":math:`a(T_{\\mathrm C}-T_0)` は正なので、ソフトモードの振動数は :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` "
"で0にならないまま転移が起こる。高温相の振動数から外挿して0になる温度 :math:`T_0` は、:math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` "
"より 低い。"
msgstr ""
"At :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` the order parameter jumps from zero to a finite"
" value. A transition in which the order parameter changes discontinuously"
" is called a **first-order transition**. At :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` the "
"curvature at :math:`\\eta=0` is positive, with value :math:`a(T_{\\mathrm"
" C}-T_0)`, so the transition occurs while the soft-mode frequency is "
"still nonzero at :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}`. The zero-frequency temperature "
":math:`T_0` obtained by extrapolation of the high-temperature frequency "
"lies below :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}`."

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:109
msgid "過冷却・過熱と転移温度のずれ"
msgstr "Supercooling, Superheating, and Shifts in the Transition Temperature"

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:111
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"1次転移では、:math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` の上下に、二つの状態の一方が極小として残る温度範囲がある（:numref:`fig-"
"landau-first-order`）。 :math:`T_0<T<T_{\\mathrm C}` では :math:`\\eta=0` の曲率"
" :math:`a(T-T_0)` が正なので、:math:`\\eta=0` は自由エネルギーの最小ではないが、 "
"極小として残る。冷却では、高温相がこの範囲まで **過冷却** されうる。逆に加熱では、:math:`\\eta\\ne0` の極小が、 "
":math:`a(T-T_0)+\\beta\\eta^2+\\gamma\\eta^4=0` が正の実数解 :math:`\\eta^2` "
"をもつ温度、すなわち"
msgstr ""
"In a first-order transition, there are temperature ranges above and below"
" :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` in which one of the two states persists as a "
"local minimum (:numref:`fig-landau-first-order`). For "
":math:`T_0<T<T_{\\mathrm C}`, the curvature at :math:`\\eta=0` is "
"positive, :math:`a(T-T_0)`, so :math:`\\eta=0` remains a local minimum "
"even though it is no longer the global minimum of the free energy. On "
"cooling, the high-temperature phase can therefore undergo "
"**supercooling** into this range. Conversely, on heating, the minimum at "
":math:`\\eta\\ne0` persists as long as "
":math:`a(T-T_0)+\\beta\\eta^2+\\gamma\\eta^4=0` has a positive real "
"solution for :math:`\\eta^2`, that is, as long as"

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:116
#, python-brace-format
msgid "T<T_1=T_0+\\frac{\\beta^2}{4a\\gamma}"
msgstr "T<T_1=T_0+\\frac{\\beta^2}{4a\\gamma}"

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:121
msgid "まで残り、低温相が **過熱** されうる。最小ではない極小にある状態を準安定な状態と呼ぶ。"
msgstr ""
"The low-temperature phase can therefore undergo **superheating**. A state"
" at a local minimum that is higher than the global minimum is called "
"metastable."

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:123
msgid "1次転移の自由エネルギー曲線。T1より上では原点だけが極小。TCとT1の間では原点が最小で、両側に浅い極小が残る。TCでは三つの極小の高さが等しい。T0とTCの間では両側の極小が最小で、原点に浅い極小が残る。T0では原点が極小でなくなる。"
msgstr ""
"Free energy curves for a first-order transition. Above T1 the origin is "
"the only minimum. Between TC and T1, the origin is the global minimum and"
" shallow local minima remain on both sides. At TC the three minima have "
"equal free energy. Between T0 and TC, the two side minima are the global "
"minima and a shallow local minimum remains at the origin. At T0 the "
"origin ceases to be a local minimum."

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:129
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
":math:`a=1`、:math:`\\beta=-1`、:math:`\\gamma=1`、:math:`T_0=0` の式 :eq"
":`landau-expansion` を、5つの温度で描いた （:math:`T_{\\mathrm "
"C}=3/16`、:math:`T_1=1/4`）。青は :math:`\\eta\\ne0` の状態が準安定な範囲、赤は "
":math:`\\eta=0` の状態が準安定な範囲。 係数は説明用で、特定の物質の値ではない。"
msgstr ""
"For :math:`a=1`, :math:`\\beta=-1`, :math:`\\gamma=1`, and :math:`T_0=0`,"
" Equation :eq:`landau-expansion` is plotted at five temperatures "
"(:math:`T_{\\mathrm C}=3/16` and :math:`T_1=1/4`). Blue indicates the "
"range in which the :math:`\\eta\\ne0` state is metastable, and red the "
"range in which the :math:`\\eta=0` state is metastable. The coefficients "
"are illustrative and do not represent any particular material."

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:133
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"準安定な状態から最小の状態へ移るには、二つの極小の間の山を越える必要がある。実際の結晶では、新しい相が核を作って "
"広がるまで、準安定な状態が残ることがある。そのため、冷却では :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` と :math:`T_0` "
"の間、加熱では :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` と :math:`T_1` "
"の間で状態が切り替わり、加熱と冷却で転移温度がずれうる（転移温度のヒステリシス）。 "
"ずれの大きさは、この範囲の中で、核の生成の起こりやすさや加熱・冷却の速さで決まる。分子動力学で加熱と冷却の 転移温度を比べるときの注意は、\\ "
":ref:`見かけの転移温度<apparent-transition-temperature>`\\ で扱う。"
msgstr ""
"A metastable state must cross the barrier between the two minima to reach"
" the global minimum. In actual crystals, the metastable state can persist"
" until the new phase nucleates and grows. As a result, the state switches"
" between :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` and :math:`T_0` on cooling and between "
":math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` and :math:`T_1` on heating. The transition "
"temperatures on heating and cooling can therefore differ (transition-"
"temperature hysteresis). The magnitude of the shift within these ranges "
"depends on how readily nucleation occurs and the rate of heating or "
"cooling. For precautions when comparing transition temperatures on "
"heating and cooling in molecular dynamics, see \\ :ref:`the apparent "
"transition temperature <apparent-transition-temperature>`\\ ."

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:142
msgid "共役な場への応答とCurie–Weissの法則"
msgstr "Response to the Conjugate Field and the Curie–Weiss Law"

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:144
msgid "秩序変数が分極 :math:`P` のとき、電場 :math:`E` を加えると自由エネルギーに :math:`-EP` が加わる。"
msgstr ""
"If the order parameter is the polarization :math:`P`, applying an "
"electric field :math:`E` adds the term :math:`-EP` to the free energy:"

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:146
msgid "F(P,T)=F_0+\\frac12a(T-T_0)P^2+\\frac14\\beta P^4+\\frac16\\gamma P^6-EP"
msgstr "F(P,T)=F_0+\\frac12a(T-T_0)P^2+\\frac14\\beta P^4+\\frac16\\gamma P^6-EP"

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:151
msgid ""
"高温相の :math:`P=0` のまわりで :math:`\\partial F/\\partial P=0` を :math:`P` "
"の1次まで残して解くと :math:`a(T-T_0)P=E` となり、 電気感受率は"
msgstr ""
"In the high-temperature phase near :math:`P=0`, solving :math:`\\partial "
"F/\\partial P=0` to linear order in :math:`P` gives :math:`a(T-T_0)P=E`, "
"and the electric susceptibility is"

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:154
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\chi=\\frac{P}{\\varepsilon_0E}=\\frac{1}{\\varepsilon_0a(T-T_0)},\\qquad"
" C=\\frac{1}{\\varepsilon_0a}"
msgstr ""
"\\chi=\\frac{P}{\\varepsilon_0E}=\\frac{1}{\\varepsilon_0a(T-T_0)},\\qquad"
" C=\\frac{1}{\\varepsilon_0a}"

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:159
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"となる。:math:`T_0` に近づくと発散するこの温度依存 :math:`\\chi=C/(T-T_0)` を "
"**Curie–Weissの法則**、:math:`C` をCurie定数、 :math:`T_0` "
"をCurie–Weiss温度と呼ぶ。Curie–Weiss温度は、2次の係数が0になる温度である。強誘電体の常誘電相での観測は 「\\ "
":ref:`ferroelectricity`\\ 」の\\ :ref:`常誘電相とキュリー温度<paraelectric-phase>`\\ "
"で扱う。2次転移ならこれは転移温度 :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` に等しく、1次転移なら :math:`T_{\\mathrm "
"C}` より低い。1次転移では、:math:`\\chi` は :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` で有限のまま転移する。 "
"極性ソフトモードの振動数とCurie–Weissの法則のつながりは、\\ :ref:`Lyddane–Sachs–Tellerの関係<polar-"
"soft-mode>`\\ で扱った。"
msgstr ""
"This temperature dependence, which diverges as the temperature approaches"
" :math:`T_0`, is :math:`\\chi=C/(T-T_0)` and is called the **Curie–Weiss "
"law**. The coefficient :math:`C` is the Curie constant and :math:`T_0` is"
" the Curie–Weiss temperature, the temperature at which the quadratic "
"coefficient vanishes. Measurements in the paraelectric phase of "
"ferroelectrics are discussed in “\\ :ref:`Ferroelectricity and Crystal "
"Structure <ferroelectricity>`\\ ”, in the section on \\ :ref:`the "
"paraelectric phase and the Curie temperature <paraelectric-phase>`\\ . "
"For a second-order transition, the Curie–Weiss temperature equals the "
"transition temperature :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}`. For a first-order "
"transition, it is below :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}`, and the transition occurs"
" with :math:`\\chi` still finite at :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}`. The \\ "
":ref:`Lyddane–Sachs–Teller relation <polar-soft-mode>`\\  section "
"discusses how the polar soft-mode frequency is related to the Curie–Weiss"
" law."

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:168
msgid "説明用の事例：BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ の立方晶–正方晶転移"
msgstr "Worked Example: Cubic-to-Tetragonal Transition in BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ "

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:170
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ の立方晶–正方晶転移は1次転移である。Merzは、転移温度のすぐ上で、弱い電場では分極が電場に比例し、 "
"強い電場では分極–電場曲線の両端にヒステリシスが開くこと（二重ヒステリシス）を観測した [Merz1953]_。 "
":math:`T>T_{\\mathrm C}` でも、:numref:`fig-landau-first-order` の青の曲線のように "
":math:`P\\ne0` の極小が近くにあれば、 電場で :math:`-EP` "
"を加えたときにその極小が最小になり、分極が跳ぶ。電場を戻すと分極が0に戻るので、正負の電場の側に 一つずつヒステリシスが開く。この観測は、式 "
":eq:`fe-devonshire` の4次の係数 :math:`\\beta` が負であることを示す。 BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ "
"の三つの転移は、いずれも1次転移である [Zhong1995]_。"
msgstr ""
"The cubic-to-tetragonal transition of BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\  is a first-"
"order transition. Just above the transition temperature, Merz observed "
"that the polarization was proportional to the electric field at weak "
"fields, but that hysteresis loops opened at both ends of the "
"polarization–field curve at strong fields (double hysteresis) "
"[Merz1953]_. Even for :math:`T>T_{\\mathrm C}`, if there is a nearby "
"minimum as on the blue curve in :numref:`fig-landau-first-order`, at "
":math:`P\\ne0`, adding the field term :math:`-EP` makes it the global "
"minimum and the polarization jumps. When the field is reduced again, the "
"polarization returns to zero, so one hysteresis loop opens on the "
"positive-field side and one on the negative-field side. This observation "
"shows that the quartic coefficient in Equation :eq:`fe-devonshire`, "
":math:`\\beta`, is negative. All three transitions in BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\"
"  are first-order transitions [Zhong1995]_."

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:177
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"1次転移では、\\ :ref:`極性ソフトモード<polar-soft-mode>`\\ の振動数は :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}`"
" で0にならず、誘電率は :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` で有限のまま転移する。:math:`T_0` "
"は、転移温度より上の誘電率や振動数を外挿して決まる温度で、 転移温度そのものではない。"
msgstr ""
"In a first-order transition, the \\ :ref:`polar soft mode <polar-soft-"
"mode>`\\  frequency does not go to zero at :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}`, and "
"the permittivity is still finite at :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` as the "
"transition takes place. The temperature :math:`T_0` comes from an "
"extrapolation of the permittivity or frequency from above the transition."
" It is not the transition temperature itself."

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:184
msgid "解釈と限界"
msgstr "Interpretation and Limitations"

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:186
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Landau理論は、秩序変数の空間的な揺らぎを無視し、平均の秩序変数だけで自由エネルギーを表す平均場の理論である。 "
"2次転移の近くで揺らぎが大きくなる系では、秩序変数が :math:`(T_0-T)^{1/2}` に比例するという予測（臨界指数1/2）が "
"実験と一致しないことがある。展開は秩序変数が小さい範囲で使えるもので、係数 "
":math:`a`、:math:`\\beta`、:math:`\\gamma` は 実験や計算に合わせて決める現象論的な量である。"
msgstr ""
"Landau theory is a mean-field theory that neglects spatial fluctuations "
"of the order parameter and expresses the free energy in terms of the "
"average order parameter alone. In systems with large fluctuations near a "
"second-order transition, the predicted proportionality of the order "
"parameter to :math:`(T_0-T)^{1/2}` (critical exponent 1/2) may disagree "
"with experiment. The expansion applies for small values of the order "
"parameter, and the coefficients :math:`a`, :math:`\\beta`, and "
":math:`\\gamma` are phenomenological quantities set by fitting to "
"experiments or calculations."

#: ../../solid/landau_theory.rst:191
msgid ""
"秩序変数が複数の成分をもつ場合（立方晶の3方向に縮退した極性モードなど）や、ひずみと結合する場合は、 対称性が許す項を展開に加える。その例は\\ "
":ref:`二重井戸ポテンシャル<double-well-potential>`\\ の式 :eq:`sm-strain` と :eq:`sm-"
"cubic-quartic` にある。"
msgstr ""
"If the order parameter has multiple components, as for a polar mode "
"degenerate along three directions in a cubic crystal, or if it couples to"
" strain, include the terms allowed by symmetry in the expansion. The \\ "
":ref:`double-well potential <double-well-potential>`\\  section gives "
"examples in Equations :eq:`sm-strain` and :eq:`sm-cubic-quartic`."

